  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 589a77387c7c4ea488d9368fe6c3cd2f, type: 3}
  m_Name: Start Dialogue
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  characterName: Axion
  dialogues:
  - Our very first step is to find a way to represent the RESOURCES in such a way
    that it preserves both what each resource is and where in the sequence the resources
    was. A transformer does this with its POSITIONAL ENCODER!
  - The POSITIONAL ENCODER takes the loose resources, represents them as a single
    matrix, EMBEDS that matrix using a NEURAL NETWORK, and finally adds positional
    information to that EMBEDDING.
  - To make a matrix from RESOURCES, each type of resource is represented as its
    own vector. The vector has dimensions equal to the amount of unique RESOURCES
    we expect to use in the factory. In our case this is seven!
  - To start building our POSITIONAL ENCODER, take the RESOURCES supplied by the
    IMPORT building and feed them into a MATRIX FACTORY to create a single matrix
    representing each resource in the sequence.
